WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.930
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:06.310
There is a strange, unexplainable phenomenon
that plagues the stock market.

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.120
It’s called the Ting Hai Effect.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:14.589
There is a huge and very sudden drop in the
stock market whenever a film or a television

00:00:14.589 --> 00:00:18.430
series staring Hong Kong actor Adam Cheng
is released.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:22.069
If this is the strangest thing you’ve ever
heard, you’re not alone.

00:00:22.069 --> 00:00:25.460
It may seem crazy but it’s completely true.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:31.689
The stock market is an enormous, global beast
that constantly goes up or goes down.

00:00:31.689 --> 00:00:36.960
Which direction it will go in the future is
determined by millions of social, economic

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.110
and political factors.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:44.030
Many of the world’s greatest mathematicians
and analysts have spent years attempting to

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:47.440
accurately predict the stock market.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.410
All have failed.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:54.460
Sudden drops in the markets are usually caused
by major news releases.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:01:00.130
The release of a new film or TV show should
have no impact whatsoever on the markets.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:07.560
Yet, despite this, on 5th October 1992 the
first episode of a TV series called the Greed

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:11.780
of Man staring Hong Kong actor Adam Cheng
was aired on TV.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:17.499
The Hang Seng Index, which measures the combined
strength of Hong Kong’s stock market, fell

00:01:17.499 --> 00:01:19.360
by 600 points.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:26.859
And then, two years later Instinct made its
TV debut, staring Adam Cheng; the Hand Seng

00:01:26.859 --> 00:01:30.560
Index fell by over 2,000 points!

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:36.650
Three years later, Adam Cheng stars in Once
Upon a Time in Shanghai, guess what… the

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:40.170
Hang Seng Index fell by 300 points.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:47.819
This happened time and time again, over 25
years and many TV and film releases.

00:01:47.819 --> 00:01:53.700
Every single time the stock market unexplainably
dropped due to Adam Cheng’s appearance in

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.249
said shows.

00:01:55.249 --> 00:01:59.420
This phenomenon has been speculated upon by
stock brokers for decades.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:06.600
No one has been able to explain the true cause
but some investors argue that the first one

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:13.860
or two occurrences were genuine coincidences
and it has since become a self-fulfilling

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.250
prophecy.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:21.350
When a great number of people believe something
to be true even if it isn’t, they can actually

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:26.480
make it happen through their subsequent actions.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:31.690
Due to the so called “Ting Hai Effect”
happening in the past, whenever a TV show

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:37.580
or film is now released staring Adam Cheng
it becomes big news in Hong Kong, especially

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:39.690
amongst financial investors.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:44.950
Because financial investors are expecting
the stock market to drop upon the show’s

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:51.500
release, they could actually be fulfilling
this prophecy and making it happen themselves,

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.630
through their investments.

00:02:53.630 --> 00:03:01.590
A one-time coincidence has thus become a regularly
occurring phenomenon, due to crowd psychology.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:06.990
If you think a Chinese film-star buggering
up the stock market is strange, you won’t

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:08.880
believe what I’m about to tell you.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:12.540
This tale of coincidence is between two American
presidents.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:16.140
None other than Abraham Lincoln and John F.
Kennedy.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:21.270
The timelines of their individual lives are
so unbelievably similar to each other that

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:26.080
many people have a hard time believing it
to be just a coincidence.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:31.760
Firstly, Abraham Lincoln was elected to Congress
in 1846.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:38.400
John F. Kennedy was elected to Congress in
1946, precisely 100 years later.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:46.120
Then Lincoln was elected President in 1860,
JFK was elected President in 1960, again,

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.080
exactly 100 years apart.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:53.700
Then both presidents and their wives lost
their children whilst living in the White

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:54.700
House.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:57.020
But it gets even weirder…

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:02.010
Both presidents were shot in the head and
both were shot dead on a Friday.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:06.770
Both men were shot in the back of the head
and in the presence of their wives.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:13.880
Lincoln was shot inside Ford’s Theatre and
Kennedy was shot in a Lincoln car, made by

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:14.880
Ford.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:20.440
When it comes to presidential coincidences
there’s something very odd going on with

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:21.440
their hands.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:25.259
10% of the global population are left handed.

00:04:25.259 --> 00:04:31.699
But that figure is massively skewed when it
comes to US presidents, 50% of the previous

00:04:31.699 --> 00:04:34.169
twelve presidents were left handed.

00:04:34.169 --> 00:04:37.130
That’s five times higher than the norm.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:40.930
Although there may be more to this than pure
coincidence.

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:46.610
Some scientists believe left-handed people
are more capable of quicker and broader thinking.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:51.259
This is backed up by the fact that a much
higher percentage of historical geniuses,

00:04:51.259 --> 00:04:56.460
Einstein, Isaac Newton and Charles Darwin,
for example, were left handed, when compared

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:57.870
to the general population.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:06.949
But there are some incredible stories of coincidences
from history that have no logical explanation.

00:05:06.949 --> 00:05:13.620
Bermuda, 1975, a man is riding a moped down
the street when suddenly a taxi, carrying

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.860
a passenger, hits him at high speed.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:18.669
He is killed instantly.

00:05:18.669 --> 00:05:25.810
Exactly one year later the dead man’s brother
is killed in the exact same way.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:30.919
And when I say the exact same way, I mean
he was driving the same moped, not a similar

00:05:30.919 --> 00:05:32.710
moped, the exact same one.

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:38.460
He was struck down in the exact same spot
by the same taxi driver and get this, the

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:43.039
taxi driver was even carrying the same passenger.

00:05:43.039 --> 00:05:46.340
To top it off, the brothers were both 17 years
old when they died.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:49.129
That’s seriously spooky.

00:05:49.129 --> 00:05:53.569
A man named Henry Ziegland knew all too well
about coincidences.

00:05:53.569 --> 00:05:56.529
In 1883 he broke up with his girlfriend.

00:05:56.529 --> 00:05:59.979
She was so upset by this she committed suicide.

00:05:59.979 --> 00:06:05.720
The girl’s brother was so angry that he
hunted down Ziegland and shot him in the head.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:10.729
The brother then immediately turned the gun
on himself and took his own life.

00:06:10.729 --> 00:06:16.840
Unaware to the deceased brother, his bullet
had not actually killed Ziegland, it narrowly

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:20.830
missed, grazing his cheek and lodged itself
in a tree behind him.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:24.159
The bullet remained in the tree for many years.

00:06:24.159 --> 00:06:30.259
Until one day Ziegland decided to chop down
the tree, it was such a hardy tree that Ziegland

00:06:30.259 --> 00:06:33.569
had to turn to dynamite to blow up the tree
instead.

00:06:33.569 --> 00:06:39.669
He blew the tree to pieces with a few sticks
of dynamite but the explosion propelled the

00:06:39.669 --> 00:06:45.710
bullet from the tree, straight into Ziegland’s
head, killing him.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:52.069
The very same bullet that was meant for his
head all those years ago.

00:06:52.069 --> 00:06:58.680
Unbelievable coincidences can sometimes follow
a single theme, for example, and this is seriously

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:04.900
weird, it turns out that lost precious rings
have a long history of turning up inside the

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:06.300
bellies of fish.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:11.210
I’ve not lost it, this is a genuine thing,
in fact, if you’ve lost your wedding ring

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:15.229
you’d be better off going fishing than actually
looking for it.

00:07:15.229 --> 00:07:22.120
Accounts of this go all the way back to 500
BC, when the fierce Tyrant of Samos, Polycrates

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:25.779
threw his gold and emerald seal-ring into
the sea.

00:07:25.779 --> 00:07:31.550
Then, six days later a fisherman brought a
fish to Polycrate’s door and presented it

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:32.550
to him.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:37.789
Whilst preparing the fish, Polycrate’s servants
cut into it and what was inside its belly?

00:07:37.789 --> 00:07:42.469
None other than the very ring he had cast
into the sea a week ago.

00:07:42.469 --> 00:07:49.349
An incredible coincidence indeed, but this
could be no more than an urban legend, it

00:07:49.349 --> 00:07:53.110
was 2,500 years ago after all.

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:58.339
But the same, remarkable coincidence has repeated
itself in recent years.

00:07:58.339 --> 00:08:04.219
Two tales come from Norway, the first tells
of a man called Waldemar Andersen.

00:08:04.219 --> 00:08:08.050
Whilst fishing in the North Sea he caught
a large cod and brought it home to prepare

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:09.050
for dinner.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:13.070
He cut open the cod’s stomach to find a
gold earring inside.

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:18.889
He gave it to his wife who was shocked, she
knew instantly that it was the earring she

00:08:18.889 --> 00:08:23.129
had lost a week earlier, when it had fallen
into the sea.

00:08:23.129 --> 00:08:29.050
There are plenty more fish in the sea but
to catch the very one that contains your wife’s

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:33.289
lost earing is nothing short of amazing.

00:08:33.289 --> 00:08:40.520
So then what if I told you the second story,
also in Norway, took place not over one week,

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:43.099
but ten years?

00:08:43.099 --> 00:08:48.860
In 1979, Robert Johansen, aged 15, was fishing
in a Norwegian fjord.

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:53.240
Like our last tale, he caught a large cod
that would be fitting for his family’s dinner

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:54.510
that evening.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:58.949
His grandmother prepared the fish back at
home and in the fish’s stomach?

00:08:58.949 --> 00:09:04.899
None other than a diamond ring, the grandmother
instantly recognized it, for it was the same

00:09:04.899 --> 00:09:11.070
valuable family heirloom she had lost in the
fjord over ten years ago.

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:17.139
And there’s more, John Cross of Virginia
lost his ring in 1980 during a vicious storm.

00:09:17.139 --> 00:09:22.240
Two years later he found it inside a fish
served up to him at his favourite restaurant

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:24.130
in Charlottesville.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:29.600
Seriously, why do people keep finding their
lost jewelry inside fish?

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:38.620
Well how about I explain exactly how in just
a moment, but first, one last remarkable story.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:45.009
The chances of you dying on a ship are extremely
low but if your name is Hugh Williams then

00:09:45.009 --> 00:09:50.320
it seems your chances of perishing at sea
are near impossible.

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:56.780
On December 5th, 1664 a ship sank in the Menai
Strait, off the coast of Wales.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:10:04.490
All 81 passengers on board died, except one,
a man named Hugh Williams.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:12.069
Then on December 5th of 1785 another ship
sank in the Menai Strait, killing all 60 people

00:10:12.069 --> 00:10:16.950
on board, except one, a man named Hugh Williams.

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:24.339
Then again on December 5th, 1820 a third ship,
guess where it sank, the Menai Strait, 25

00:10:24.339 --> 00:10:27.990
people drowned, guess who was the only survivor…

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:30.459
Hugh Williams.

00:10:30.459 --> 00:10:34.130
If that’s not enough to float your coincidental
boat, get this.

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:40.230
On 10th July 1940, a British trawler was destroyed
by a German mine.

00:10:40.230 --> 00:10:46.899
Only two men survived the catastrophe, both
were named Hugh Williams.

00:10:46.899 --> 00:10:50.389
Coincidence seems to favour misfortune.

00:10:50.389 --> 00:10:55.509
Nothing exemplifies this more than the fact
that four of the world’s most infamous leaders,

00:10:55.509 --> 00:11:02.730
worst dictators and genocidal maniacs to have
ever lived, Adolf Hitler, Josef Stalin, Leon

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:13.220
Trotsky, Josip Tito and Sigmund Freud all
share something in common, a very eerie coincidence.

00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:21.160
All five men lived in Vienna at the exact
same time, before they all became infamous.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:26.870
They all walked through the same park every
day and regularly drank at the same coffee

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:27.870
shop.

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:32.560
The five men didn’t know each other before
moving to or spending time in Vienna, some

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:37.250
of them even met whilst living in Vienna and
hatched their ambitious plans together to

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:40.050
revolutionise the world in their own image.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:46.589
But these are the five men who collectively
changed the history of Europe and the world

00:11:46.589 --> 00:11:52.949
more than anyone before them, of the thousands
of cities in Europe, what are the chances

00:11:52.949 --> 00:11:59.410
of them all residing in the same city and
frequenting the same coffee shop?

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:04.370
What are the chances of five sole survivors
of shipwrecks in the same location, on the

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:09.470
same day of the same month, being called the
same name?

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:14.079
And for goodness sake, what are the chances
of numerous people finding their lost jewelry

00:12:14.079 --> 00:12:15.810
inside fish?

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:21.050
What are the chances that a man will be hit
in the head by a bullet, flying from the explosion

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:26.050
of a tree; the same bullet shot at his head
many years ago?

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:31.440
What are the chances that numerous presidents
share so many, very close similarities?

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:38.269
And we all want to know, what are the chances
of a Chinese man disrupting the stock market

00:12:38.269 --> 00:12:40.310
with his acting?

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:42.529
Well quite high actually.

00:12:42.529 --> 00:12:48.759
The chances of each of these apparently highly
unlikely events happening to you is minutely

00:12:48.759 --> 00:12:56.519
small, but the chance of it happening to someone
in the world is very, very high indeed, almost

00:12:56.519 --> 00:12:57.880
100% in fact.

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:03.790
We’ve all heard of the law of large numbers
but Harvard mathematicians Persi Diaconis

00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:10.399
and Fred Mostellar created a new law called
the “Law of truly large numbers”.

00:13:10.399 --> 00:13:17.129
Which states that given a sample size large
enough, any outrageous and unimaginable thing

00:13:17.129 --> 00:13:22.279
is highly likely to happen, despite how unbelievable
it may be.

00:13:22.279 --> 00:13:26.949
Just like how the infinite monkey theorem
states that a room full of monkeys randomly

00:13:26.949 --> 00:13:34.000
hitting keys on typewriters, will, given long
enough, eventually type out the complete works

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.300
of William Shakespeare.

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:42.300
We don’t find likely, everyday events particularly
remarkable, quite the opposite, we ignore

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:43.300
them.

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:48.759
But we do highlight unlikely occurrences,
making them seem inherently more remarkable.

00:13:48.759 --> 00:13:54.040
Say you’re running a simulation where the
chance of a particular event occurring is

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:55.040
0.1%.

00:13:55.040 --> 00:14:02.839
Therefore, the probability that this highly
unlikely event will NOT happen is 99.9%.

00:14:02.839 --> 00:14:10.509
But if you repeated the simulation 1,000 times,
the chance that that event will not happen

00:14:10.509 --> 00:14:17.600
at least once is 0.999 to the power of 1,000,
or 36.8%.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:27.500
And so the chance of that event occurring
once in 1,000 simulations is now 63.2%, a

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:28.500
bit different from 0.1%.

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:41.470
Run the simulation 10,000 times and the chance
of that unlikely event happening is now 99.995%.

00:14:41.470 --> 00:14:47.310
If two omnipotent mice are to be believed,
then planet Earth is one giant simulation

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:53.509
and there are over 7 billion participants
running their own simulations every day by

00:14:53.509 --> 00:14:56.000
simply living out their lives.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:01.800
The chance of something truly remarkable and
highly coincidental happening amongst 7 billion

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:05.439
people’s lives is almost 100%.

00:15:05.439 --> 00:15:09.200
Given a large enough sample set, ie.

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:14.850
the human race, anything that can happen will
happen, eventually.

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:20.940
But of course, when those very special and
seemingly miraculous events do occur, they

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:26.379
get global media attention giving them a very
high level of recognition.

00:15:26.379 --> 00:15:32.120
Yet we pay no attention to the billions of
uneventful things that happen around the world

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:33.910
every day.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:39.910
Roughly 7 billion fish are caught from the
wild every day by humans, and probably not

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:43.160
one of them contained someone’s missing
diamond ring.

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:47.519
But when you think about the sheer scale of
the world and its inhabitants and all the

00:15:47.519 --> 00:15:53.389
trillions of things they collectively do each
day, the fact that someone didn’t find their

00:15:53.389 --> 00:16:00.949
lost diamond ring inside a fish today, never
mind this past year, actually seems more unbelievable

00:16:00.949 --> 00:16:02.550
than if someone did.

00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:05.410
Thanks for watching.

